 "final_message": "I've made all twelve changes, and the six tests in the suite pass (the four existing ones plus the two new ones). I didn't write tests for the other fixes, so those are untested beyond the suite.\n\n- **Sections 1\u20137:** I fixed `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` to match the spec. The line numbers in `ValueError` messages count skipped lines.\n- **Tests:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **README:** I corrected the `conversions_in_window` entry and added one for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n- **Other package fixes (item 12):**\n  - `top_converting_groups` now breaks ties by group name and excludes groups with no sessions.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now returns `None` for empty groups and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` wasn't resetting its run count after a day with no flagged sessions, so I fixed that.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise a `ValueError` naming the line in that case. Say if you'd rather it handle those values differently.",
